 j : Nat} (h : LT.lt.{0} (HAdd.hAdd.{0, 0, 0} i j) (List.length.{u_1} xs)),\n  Eq.{u_1 + 1} (GetElem.getElem.{u_1, 0, u_1} xs (HAdd.hAdd.{0, 0, 0} i j) h)\n    (GetElem.getElem.{u_1, 0, u_1} (List.drop.{u_1} i xs) j ⋯)","unsafe":false,"value":407,"source":{"code":"/-- The `i + j`-th element of a list coincides with the `j`-th element of the list obtained by\ndropping the first `i` elements. Version designed to rewrite from the big list to the small list. -/\ntheorem getElem_drop' {xs : List α} {i j : Nat} (h : i + j < xs.length) :\n    xs[i + j] = (xs.drop i)[j]'(lt_length_drop h) := by\n  have : i ≤ xs.length := Nat.le_trans (Nat.le_add_right _ _) (Nat.le_of_lt h)\n  rw [getElem_of_eq (take_append_drop i xs).symm h, getElem_append_right]\n  · simp [Nat.min_eq_left this, Nat.add_sub_cancel_left]\n  · simp [Nat.min_eq_left this, Nat.le_add_right]","start":223,"end":230},"axioms":["propext"]}